1.Introduction
Recent advances are increasingly positioning large language models (LLMs) as general-purpose reasoners, capable of solving problems that require multi-step deduction, intermediate decisions, and long-horizon planning. While eliciting explicit intermediate reasoning steps (Chain-of-Thought) Wei et al.(2023) substantially improves accuracy, reasoning stability remains a central bottleneck
