H.Additional Results on Thinking Models
To further examine whether PoT complements models with built-in long-form reasoning, we evaluate it on two dedicated thinking models: Qwen3-4B-Thinking-2507 and Qwen3-30B-Thinking-2507.
As shown in Table17, PoT consistently improves both models. On Qwen3-4B-Thinking-2507, PoT increases LCB V6 accuracy from 55.20 to 63.70 (+8.50 points). On Qwen3-30B-Thinking-2507, accuracy improves from 76.80 to 84.90 (+8.10 points).
These gains indicate that PoT is complementary to native reasoning capabilities rather than a substitute. Even when the base model already performs extended multi-step reasoning, test-time policy evolution remains beneficial by refining reasoning trajectories using environment feedback and adapting the policy to the current instance.
